  "attack_progression": [
    {"step": 1, "tactic": "Initial Access / Phishing — Spearphishing via Service", "technique": "T1566.003", "what_happened": "At 2026-05-13 09:14:07 CEST, Wazuh rule 91420 'SMS phishing relay API call from corp endpoint' fired on agent WIN-FIN-118 (10.108.57.177). An outbound HTTP POST was sent from the corporate endpoint to the internal SMS gateway API at http://10.108.57.40/api/sms/send. The POST body carried a corp-themed smishing lure: 'Corp IT: Your VPN token expires in 2h. Renew at http://10.108.57.177/vpn/renew?u=alice'. The User-Agent was 'Twilio/SmsApi-1.0', mimicking the Twilio SDK default UA to blend with legitimate messaging traffic. Two further POSTs followed within 4 minutes carrying an HR-bonus lure and a fake security-alert lure, each targeting a different internal phone extension (+15550101001, +15550101002, +15550101003).", "chain_reason": "Wazuh rule 91420 (rule.mitre.id T1566.003) triggered with the smishing message body captured in rule.description. The corp endpoint is generating outbound HTTP POSTs to an SMS-send API endpoint — a workstation has no business calling an SMS gateway send API directly.", "first_seen": "2026-05-13T09:14:07+0200"},
    {"step": 2, "tactic": "Initial Access / Phishing — Spearphishing via Service", "technique": "T1566.003", "what_happened": "Between 09:16 and 09:19 CEST, Wazuh rule 91421 'Outbound SMS gateway request from workstation' fired three times on the same agent WIN-FIN-118. These POSTs hit a second gateway path http://10.108.57.40/messaging/v1/sms with a different User-Agent 'VonageClient/7.4.0 (Java)' — the operator is fanning the smishing relay across multiple gateway endpoints and SDK personas to maximise delivery and evade single-signature detection. Same three corp-themed lures, same three phone extensions.", "chain_reason": "Wazuh rule 91421 (rule.mitre.id T1566.003) fired repeatedly from a single workstation agent against an internal SMS gateway. Multiple SDK User-Agents (Twilio + Vonage) from one endpoint within minutes is scripted relay behaviour, not human messaging-app use.", "first_seen": "2026-05-13T09:16:12+0200"},
    {"step": 3, "tactic": "Initial Access / Phishing — Spearphishing via Service", "technique": "T1660", "what_happened": "At 09:19:32 CEST, Suricata logged a DNS query for api.twilio.com followed by a TLS ClientHello with SNI=api.twilio.com, sourced from data.srcip=10.108.57.177. The corp endpoint attempted an outbound POST to https://api.twilio.com/2010-04-01/Accounts/.../Messages.json — an attempt to relay the smishing campaign through the real Twilio cloud SMS API. The request returned HTTP 401 (no valid Twilio credentials) but the DNS + TLS SNI artefacts confirm the operator is escalating from the internal gateway to a public SMS provider to scale delivery beyond the corp network.", "chain_reason": "Suricata DNS (data.dns.rrname=api.twilio.com) + TLS SNI (data.tls.sni=api.twilio.com) + HTTP request with data.srcip=10.108.57.177 to a known SMS-provider API. The 401 confirms an unauthorised relay attempt — the operator does not yet hold Twilio credentials but is actively probing the channel.", "first_seen": "2026-05-13T09:19:32+0200"},
    {"step": 4, "tactic": "Initial Access / Phishing — Cumulative Smishing Relay Campaign", "technique": "T1566.003", "what_happened": "Across the 09:14-09:25 CEST window (~11 minutes), Wazuh aggregated 6 smishing-relay alerts from agent WIN-FIN-118 (10.108.57.177) — 3 on rule 91420 and 3 on rule 91421 — all carrying corp-themed credential-harvest lures pointing victims to http://10.108.57.177/vpn/renew, /hr/bonuses and /verify on the compromised endpoint itself. The endpoint is simultaneously the relay source AND the credential-harvest landing host. This is a self-contained internal smishing operation: compromise one corp box, use it to blast phish SMS at colleagues, and host the AiTM credential-capture pages on the same box.", "chain_reason": "Wazuh correlation across rule.id 91420 + 91421 with rule.mitre.id T1566.003 from a single agent within an 11-minute window. The lure URLs in rule.description all resolve to the relay source IP itself — the compromised endpoint is both sender and phishing-page host.", "first_seen": "2026-05-13T09:24:51+0200"}
  ],
